import QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup

/-!
# The braid tower, and Markov move II on braids

`QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup` built the braid group and its representation into the Hecke units,
and gave **Markov move I** on braids (`braidTrace_conj`). This file adds the other half: the
tower `B_{m+1} ↪ B_{m+2}` and **move II**, the peel.

## The three squares

Each layer of the arc now has its own tower map, and they commute:

| level | map |
|---|---|
| braids | `braidTower : B_{m+1} →* B_{m+2}`, `σ_a ↦ σ_{a.castSucc}` |
| algebra | `MarkovPeel.tower : H_{m+1}(q) →ₐ H_{m+2}(q)` |
| matrices | `MarkovPeel.extendSiteHom : X ↦ X ⊗ 1` |

`heckeRep_braidTower` closes the first square (`braidTower` against `tower`, through
`heckeRep`); `MarkovPeel.heckeActionN_tower` already closed the second. All three are proved the
same way — two homomorphisms agreeing on generators — and each of the three is a presentation or
a universal property doing the work rather than an induction.

The single input on the braid side is `MarkovPeel.coxA_castSucc`: the type-`A` Coxeter matrix
restricts along `castSucc`, so the relations of `B_{m+1}` are among the relations of `B_{m+2}`.

## Move II

`braidTrace_peel` — adding a strand and one crossing multiplies the trace by `z · wi`, the
normalised peel scalar. At the weight `MarkovPeel` forces, that scalar is `q³/(q²+1)`
(`braidTrace_peel_physical`), i.e. convention D's Markov parameter.

## 🛑 What is still between this and the Jones polynomial

Both Markov moves now hold for `braidTrace`. That is **not** a link invariant, and the two
missing pieces are named rather than hypothesised, because writing either as a hypothesis would
hide how much it is doing:

1. **The writhe normalisation.** Moves II⁺ and II⁻ carry *different* scalars — `σ` and `σ⁻¹` do
   not peel to the same thing — so the raw functional is an invariant of a *framed* braid
   closure. The standard fix rescales by `(something)^{writhe}`, which needs the exponent sum of
   a braid word, hence a well-defined writhe on `ArtinGroup`. Not done here.
2. **Markov's theorem.** That closure-equivalence of braids is generated by exactly these two
   moves is a theorem of low-dimensional topology. Mathlib has no braid group at all, so it
   certainly has not got this, and nothing here proves it.

Neither gap is formal bookkeeping; both are real, and this file stops at the honest boundary.

-- Ref: [jones1987] Hecke algebra representations of braid groups and link polynomials
-- Ref: [leitner2026] bean qou-k4oq
-/

namespace QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower

open QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke QOU.MathlibExt.SkeinRelation
open QOU.IwahoriHecke.Balanced QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbed
open QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidGroup QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel

variable {B : Type*} {M : B → B → ℕ}

/-! ## The braid relation holds in the presented group -/

/-- **The defining relation, in the group.** The alternating words agree in `Art(M)` — which is
what `PresentedGroup` was quotiented by, read back through `map_altProd`. -/
theorem braidGen_braid (M : B → B → ℕ) (i j : B) :
    altProd (braidGen M i) (braidGen M j) (M i j)
      = altProd (braidGen M j) (braidGen M i) (M j i) := by
  have h : PresentedGroup.mk (artinRels M) (altProd (FreeGroup.of i) (FreeGroup.of j) (M i j))
      = PresentedGroup.mk (artinRels M) (altProd (FreeGroup.of j) (FreeGroup.of i) (M j i)) :=
    PresentedGroup.mk_eq_mk_of_mul_inv_mem ⟨i, j, rfl⟩
  rw [map_altProd, map_altProd] at h
  exact h

/-! ## The tower on braids -/

variable {m : ℕ}

/-- **The braid tower** `B_{m+1} → B_{m+2}`: add a strand on the right, leaving every crossing
where it was. Its only input is `coxA_castSucc`. -/
def braidTower : BraidGroupN m →* BraidGroupN (m + 1) :=
  PresentedGroup.toGroup (f := fun a : Fin m => braidGen (coxA (m + 1)) a.castSucc) (by
    rintro r ⟨i, j, rfl⟩
    rw [map_mul, map_inv, map_altProd, map_altProd]
    simp only [FreeGroup.lift_apply_of]
    rw [← coxA_castSucc i j, ← coxA_castSucc j i, braidGen_braid, mul_inv_cancel])

@[simp] theorem braidTower_gen (a : Fin m) :
    braidTower (braidGen (coxA m) a) = braidGen (coxA (m + 1)) a.castSucc :=
  PresentedGroup.toGroup.of _

/-! ## The square: braid tower against algebra tower -/

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] (q qi : R)

/-- **The tower square commutes.** Representing a braid after adding a strand is the same as
adding the strand in the algebra — two group homomorphisms agreeing on generators. -/
theorem heckeRep_braidTower (hqi : q * qi = 1) (β : BraidGroupN m) :
    ((heckeRep (coxA (m + 1)) hqi coxA_symm (braidTower β)
        : (BalancedHecke (coxA (m + 1)) q)ˣ) : BalancedHecke (coxA (m + 1)) q)
      = tower q qi hqi
          ((heckeRep (coxA m) hqi coxA_symm β : (BalancedHecke (coxA m) q)ˣ)
            : BalancedHecke (coxA m) q) := by
  have hcomp : (heckeRep (coxA (m + 1)) hqi coxA_symm).comp (braidTower (m := m))
      = (Units.map (tower q qi hqi : BalancedHecke (coxA m) q →ₐ[R]
            BalancedHecke (coxA (m + 1)) q).toMonoidHom).comp
          (heckeRep (coxA m) hqi coxA_symm) := by
    refine PresentedGroup.ext (fun a => ?_)
    simp only [MonoidHom.comp_apply]
    rw [show (PresentedGroup.of a : BraidGroupN m) = braidGen (coxA m) a from rfl,
      braidTower_gen, heckeRep_braidGen, heckeRep_braidGen]
    refine Units.ext ?_
    rw [Units.coe_map]
    exact (tower_sigma q qi hqi a).symm
  have h := DFunLike.congr_fun hcomp β
  simp only [MonoidHom.comp_apply] at h
  rw [h, Units.coe_map]
  rfl

/-! ## Move II -/

/-- **Markov move II, on braids.** Adding a strand and one crossing multiplies the normalised
trace by the peel scalar `z · wi`. -/
theorem braidTrace_peel (hqi : q * qi = 1) (w : Fin 2 → R) (wi : R) (z : R)
    (hP : ∀ u : Fin 2, (∑ t : Fin 2, w t * RMatrix.rCheck q qi (u, t) (u, t)) = z)
    (β : BraidGroupN m) :
    braidTrace q qi hqi w wi
        (braidTower β * braidGen (coxA (m + 1)) (Fin.last m))
      = (z * wi) * braidTrace q qi hqi w wi β := by
  rw [braidTrace, braidTrace, map_mul, Units.val_mul, heckeRep_braidTower q qi hqi,
    heckeRep_braidGen_val,
    QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovNormalized.markovTr_peel q qi hqi w wi z hP]

/-- **Move II at the forced weight.** With `w = (1, q²)` — the weight the peel itself forces —
the scalar is `q³ · wi`, i.e. convention D's `z = q³/(q² + 1)`. -/
theorem braidTrace_peel_physical (hqi : q * qi = 1) (w : Fin 2 → R) (wi : R)
    (h0 : w 0 = 1) (h1 : w 1 = q ^ 2) (β : BraidGroupN m) :
    braidTrace q qi hqi w wi
        (braidTower β * braidGen (coxA (m + 1)) (Fin.last m))
      = (q ^ 3 * wi) * braidTrace q qi hqi w wi β :=
  braidTrace_peel q qi hqi w wi (q ^ 3) (peel_scalar_of_physical q qi hqi w h0 h1) β

end QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidTower
